  "verbalization": "Patupilone is linked to DMS-273 through a series of target relationships, with the most direct pathway involving MEL-HO, which is targeted by Alpinone 3-acetate, and then by DMS-273. Another pathway connects Patupilone to TE-9, which targets the same compound that also targets DMS-273. A third pathway links Patupilone to MC116, which also targets the same compound and ultimately leads to DMS-273. These findings suggest that Patupilone may act through a common mechanism that involves the activation of [(1R)-1-[(5Z)-4-Bromo-5-(Bromomethylidene)-2-Oxofuran-3-Yl]Butyl] Acetate, which in turn targets DMS-273. The evidence supports a potential role for Patupilone in modulating a pathway that involves this compound, though the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
